  "body": "From the contributor's real-control run of #521 / PR #583 on a 770MX (2026-11-09).\n\n**Today:** a G21 (mm) program posted for an inch-native PathPilot machine leaves the control in G21 after `M30`. In LinuxCNC, M2/M30 reset several modal groups but not units. The operator's DRO and MDI then stay in mm until they type `G20`.\n\n**Proposal:** a post option, default off for byte-identical output, that ends the program in the machine's native unit (from the .mch unit) by writing `G20` or `G21` before `M30` when it differs from the program's unit. Alternatively, a closing comment telling the operator which units the control was left in. Check this against the LinuxCNC M2/M30 documentation, which lists what is reset.\n\n**Done means:** with the option on, a mm program for an inch machine ends with `G20` before `M30`, and nothing changes when the units already match; with the option off, output is unchanged.\n\nRelated: #521, #583, #258 (Post dialog options).",
